ion for case: Foster, Evans and Huffington v. State\">503 A. 2d 1326</a></span>; No. 85-6749, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"464819\"><a href=\"/opinion/464819/chester-lee-wicker-v-ol-mccotter-director-texas-department-of/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Chester Lee Wicker v. O.L. McCotter Director, Texas...\">783 F. 2d 487</a></span>; No. 85-6846, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9741013\"><a href=\"/opinion/2225858/wallace-v-state/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Wallace v. State\">486 N. E. 2d 445</a></span>; No. 85-6891, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1745003\"><a href=\"/opinion/1745003/gall-v-commonwealth/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Gall v. Commonwealth\">702 S. W. 2d 37</a></span>.</p>\n</opinion>"},{"id":9054792,"type":"dissent","typeCode":"040dissent","perCuriam":false,"author":"Brennanmarshall","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":596,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"dissent\">\n<author id=\"b934-16\">Justice Brennan and Justice Marshall,</author>\n<p id=\"AdT\">dissenting.</p>\n<p id=\"b934-17\">Adhering to our views that the death penalty is in all circumstances cruel and unusual punishment prohibited by the Eighth and Fourteenth Amendments, <em>Gregg </em>v. <em>Georgia, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9426555\"><a href=\"/opinion/109532/gregg-v-georgia/#227\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Gregg v. Georgia\">428 U. S. 153, 227, 231</a></span> (1976), we would grant certiorari and vacate the death sentences in these cases.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}